<%# The guide's library form, on GK GUI Stuff's library (gk_gui_stuff_library), the same form as the icon library: the
    search, the groups as choice pills with their counts, one item per element of the register with a small picture of
    its first state (a still copy of the first tile's example, scaled down), Rutnät or Lista, and the panel of the
    element chosen: its name, plugin and number of states, the choices light or dark and computer or phone, the large
    picture of its first state, Används för and Inte för, every state as its tile with its code and Prova, and what goes
    with it (a Redmine form's GK counterpart, the Redmine forms a GK element stands for). The panel's head has the
    element's short legend after the name: the plugin, the number of states and the tiles' flags counted, whose rows frame the tiles' flags of their kind, and the item's name says the same to a screen reader, since its small picture is hidden from it. A wide element opens under the
    grid. The elements are drawn by the same partials as the page form (gk_gui_stuff_sg_draw); the anchors are the same,
    so that a link to an element works in both forms. data-gk-gui-sg-frame and data-gk-gui-sg-dark as in the page form.
    The page's bar first, as in the page form: light or dark and computer or phone for every element, and Visa all kod. %>
<% items = sections.map do |s|
     drawn = gk_gui_stuff_sg_draw(s, locals)
     body = capture do %>
       <div class="gk-gui-stuff-sg-lib-element" data-gk-gui-sg-element="<%= s.key %>" data-gk-gui-sg-group="<%= s.group %>">
         <%= gk_gui_stuff_library_preview(from: '.gk-gui-stuff-sg-shown') %>
         <%= gk_gui_stuff_sg_uses(s) %>
         <div class="gk-gui-stuff-sg-body"><%= drawn[:body] %></div>
         <%= gk_gui_stuff_sg_related(s, sections) %>
       </div>
     <% end
     { key: s.key, anchor: s.anchor, name: s.label, group: s.group, words: [s.uses, *drawn[:states]].join(' '), wide: s.wide,
       facts: [s.plugin_name, l(:label_gk_gui_stuff_sg_n_states, count: drawn[:n])], summary: gk_gui_stuff_sg_mode_summary(drawn[:modes]),
       legend: gk_gui_stuff_sg_element_legend(s, drawn[:n], drawn[:modes], area: %([data-gk-gui-sg-element="#{s.key}"])),
       tools: content_tag(:p, gk_gui_stuff_sg_tools(s, dark: @dark.present?), class: 'gk-gui-stuff-sg-lib-tools', data: { gk_gui_lib_head_tools: '1' }),
       thumb_from: '.gk-gui-stuff-sg-shown', body: body }
   end %>
<div class="gk-gui-stuff-sg-page gk-gui-stuff-sg-lib gk-gui-stuff-lib-tokens" data-gk-gui-sg-page data-gk-gui-sg-frame="<%= gk_gui_stuff_styleguide_frame_path(key: '__key__') %>" data-gk-gui-sg-nowhere="<%= l(:text_gk_gui_stuff_sg_nowhere) %>"<% if @dark %> data-gk-gui-sg-dark="<%= @dark.join(' ') %>"<% end %>>
  <%= gk_gui_stuff_sg_page_tools(dark: @dark.present?) %>
  <%= gk_gui_stuff_library('styleguide', items, groups: GkGuiStuff::Styleguide.menu(sections).map { |g| { key: g[:key], title: g[:title] } },
                           title: l(:label_gk_gui_stuff_sg_menu), search: l(:text_gk_gui_stuff_sg_search), empty: l(:text_gk_gui_stuff_sg_nothing_found)) %>
</div>
